 110:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   *** SD Card Read operation ***
 111:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   ==============================
 112:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
 113:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can read from SD card in polling mode by using function HAL_SD_ReadBlocks().
 114:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 115:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 116:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 117:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 118:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 119:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 120:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 121:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can read from SD card in DMA mode by using function HAL_SD_ReadBlocks_DMA().
 122:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 123:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 124:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 125:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 126:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 127:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 128:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You could also check the DMA transfer process through the SD Rx interrupt event.
 129:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 130:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can read from SD card in Interrupt mode by using function HAL_SD_ReadBlocks_IT().
 131:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 132:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 133:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 134:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 135:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 136:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 137:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You could also check the IT transfer process through the SD Rx interrupt event.
