 207:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   *** Callback registration ***
 208:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   =============================================
 209:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
 210:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     The compilation define USE_HAL_SD_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
 211:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
 212:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 213:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     Use Functions HAL_SD_RegisterCallback() to register a user callback,
 214:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     it allows to register following callbacks:
 215:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) TxCpltCallback : callback when a transmission transfer is completed.
 216:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) RxCpltCallback : callback when a reception transfer is completed.
 217:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) ErrorCallback : callback when error occurs.
 218:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) AbortCpltCallback : callback when abort is completed.
 219:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) MspInitCallback    : SD MspInit.
 220:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) MspDeInitCallback  : SD MspDeInit.
 221:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
 222:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     and a pointer to the user callback function.
 223:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 224:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     Use function HAL_SD_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to the default
 225:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     weak (surcharged) function. It allows to reset following callbacks:
 226:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) TxCpltCallback : callback when a transmission transfer is completed.
 227:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) RxCpltCallback : callback when a reception transfer is completed.
 228:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) ErrorCallback : callback when error occurs.
 229:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) AbortCpltCallback : callback when abort is completed.
 230:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) MspInitCallback    : SD MspInit.
 231:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) MspDeInitCallback  : SD MspDeInit.
 232:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     This function) takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle and the Callback ID.
 233:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 234:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     By default, after the HAL_SD_Init and if the state is HAL_SD_STATE_RESET
 235:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     all callbacks are reset to the corresponding legacy weak (surcharged) functions.
 236:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit callbacks that are respectively
 237:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     reset to the legacy weak (surcharged) functions in the HAL_SD_Init
 238:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     and  HAL_SD_DeInit only when these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 239:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_SD_Init and HAL_SD_DeInit
 240:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand)
 241:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 242:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in READY state only.
 243:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     Exception done for MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks that can be registered/unregistered
 244:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     in READY or RESET state, thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used
 245:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     during the Init/DeInit.
 246:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 247:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     using HAL_SD_RegisterCallback before calling HAL_SD_DeInit
 248:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     or HAL_SD_Init function.
 249:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 250:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     When The compilation define USE_HAL_SD_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 251:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     not defined, the callback registering feature is not available
 252:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****     and weak (surcharged) callbacks are used.
 253:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 254:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_sd.c ****   @endverbatim
